          "id": "d",
          "text": "$x = \\frac{3 - y}{y - 1}$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "Multiply by $(x-1)$: $y(x-1) = x + 3$. Expand: $yx - y = x + 3$. Collect $x$ terms: $yx - x = y + 3$. Factor: $x(y-1) = y + 3$. Divide: $x = \\frac{y+3}{y-1}$."
